# Configuration and secrets. config.json is the only config file Toda
# reads; config.example.json is the tracked, redacted template.
config.json
!config.example.json
# Toda no longer reads .env, but stray ones still turn up in a working
# tree and hold real credentials. Keep ignoring them so an `add -A` can
# never sweep one into a commit.
.env
.env.*

# Python tooling caches and build artifacts
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Web console build outputs (React + Vite under web/)
web/node_modules/
web/dist/
web/*.tsbuildinfo
src/toda/static/console/

# macOS
.DS_Store
node_modules/

# Toda runtime state and local operator material
data/
!src/toda/data/
!src/toda/data/models_catalog.json
!src/toda/data/models_catalog.provenance.json
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Private research/reference worktrees and generated product experiments
harnesses/
build/
dist/
imgs/
landing/
site/

# Superseded planning docs and research notes. Never tracked; kept on disk
# only as a record of how the thinking went. See archive/README.md.
archive/

# Working notes are not part of the community distribution. These are the
# documents written while building a change -- plans, handoffs, audits, the
# running understanding of a subsystem. They go stale the moment the code
# lands, and a reader who trusts one is worse off than a reader who had
# nothing. What ships is the as-built set: README, ARCHITECTURE, SECURITY,
# CONTRIBUTING and the guides under docs/.
#
# Suffix patterns rather than a list of filenames, because the list only
# ever caught the notes that already existed. All of these are also
# deliberately safe against the docs that DO ship: `*_REVIEW.md` cannot
# match SECURITY.md, `*_ARCHITECTURE.md` cannot match ARCHITECTURE.md.
*_PLAN.md
*_HANDOFF.md
*_TODO.md
*_REVIEW.md
*_AUDIT.md
*_FINDINGS.md
*_STATUS.md
*_NOTES.md
*_ADOPTION.md
*_IMPLEMENTATION.md
*_REMEDIATION.md
*_UNDERSTANDING.md
*_ARCHITECTURE.md
*_architecture.md
*ANALYSIS*.md
HARNESS_*.md
notes/
scratch/

# Agent and tool state, none of it portable to another machine
CLAUDE.md
.claude/
.commandcode/

# Other harnesses cloned for reference (OpenMausBot and friends). Whole
# third-party repositories, with their own git history and licences.
harnesses/

# Eval corpora and results. The generator, cases and scorers are tracked;
# the generated organization and every run's scores are not -- corpora are
# model-written and large, and results are per-machine.
evals/data/
evals/results/
